# ACLs for the password listener (8884, host 18884) of the secure Mosquitto in
# compose.mqtt.secure.yaml. Test-only users; their passwords are in that file.
#
# Each user owns one topic tree, the prefix its tests run under, and nothing
# else. How Mosquitto 2.1's acl_file plugin enforces it, as tests/mqtt_e2e.rs
# observes:
#
#   publish elsewhere     refused, PUBACK reason 0x87 (not authorized)
#   subscribe elsewhere   granted in the SUBACK, but every message on it fails
#                         the read check and is never delivered
#   shared subscriptions  checked the same way, against the topic each message
#                         was published on, so `$share/<group>/e2e-app/...`
#                         needs nothing beyond the read grant below
#
# Mosquitto has no topic-level refusal at SUBSCRIBE time in this plugin; the
# dynamic-security plugin's subscribe ACLs are what would turn the SUBACK into
# 0x87.

user e2e-app
topic readwrite e2e-app/#

user e2e-other
topic readwrite e2e-other/#
